# There's also a concrete bug in your smoke test

You sent:

```json
{
  "worker_id": "smoke-fast",
  "model": "opencode-go/mimo-v2.5",
  "persona": "...",
  "reasoning_effort": "none"
}
```

But `/workers` currently parses:

```ts
{
  worker_id: string;
  model?: string;
  persona?: string;
  skills?: string[];
}
```

There is **no `reasoning_effort` field**.

Then you hard-code:

```ts
reasoningEffort: "none"
```

inside `createAgent()`.

So the supplied setting from your experiment was ignored. The saved worker mapping also doesn't record it.

That is exactly the kind of thing MWGym must prevent: every treatment variable needs to be explicitly recorded in the WorkerGenome and receipt.

