# `maxSteps: 2` is also suspect

You're using:

```ts
createSession(..., {
    ...
    stateless: true,
    maxSteps: 2,
})
```

Your project has `@letta-ai/letta-agent-sdk` 0.8.0 installed.

I checked the v0.8.0 public TypeScript definitions.

`stateless` exists.

`reasoningEffort` exists.

I cannot find **`maxSteps` in the public session options at all**.

And because you're starting this using:

```text
npx tsx src/index.ts
```

you're transpiling/running rather than necessarily doing a complete TypeScript type-check first.

So I would currently treat:

```ts
maxSteps: 2
```

as **unproven / probably ignored**, until an actual run reports its agent-step count dropping to ≤2.

Don't rely on that patch as a control mechanism yet.

