# And absolutely do not put Letta inside every YGO move

This is probably the biggest architectural point for `mwgym`.

If you did:

```text
100,000 games
× maybe 100 decision points/game
× 20-35 seconds/Letta decision
```

the benchmark would be useless.

Instead:

```text
              ygoenv / ygopro-core
                 FAST INNER LOOP
                        │
                        ▼
                    game state
                        │
                  legal actions
                        │
                        ▼
                routine policy
                        │
                   uncertainty?
                    /        \
                  no          yes
                  │            │
                  ▼            ▼
                 ACT       MW ALLOCATOR
                               │
           ┌───────────────────┼───────────────────┐
           ▼                   ▼                   ▼
       Hydra lookup        rollouts          Letta/MiMo
       ~cheap/local        local CPU          expensive
           │                   │                   │
           └───────────────────┼───────────────────┘
                               ▼
                              ACT
```

This is much more representative of real autonomous work anyway.

Most actions in real jobs should **not** invoke maximum intelligence.

