# Same with learning

Your existing runtime has operations where you ask the Letta agent to reflect/update its memory.

That is useful, but don't do it after every episode.

For MWGym:

```text
game 1
game 2
game 3
...
game 100
   │
   ▼
trajectory batch
   │
   ▼
Trace2Skill / reflection
   │
candidate lessons
   │
validate
   │
   ▼
promote into Git/MemFS
```

Then:

```text
game 101 → 200
```

tests whether those changes actually improved the worker.

Otherwise we'd be spending more compute **learning from YGO than playing YGO**, while simultaneously making attribution impossible.

